eight news now along with our sister  stations all across the country  are working to tackle hunger in every  community it's the super bowl of caring  and we've shared with you that our goal  is to raise enough money to feed one  million people  in need earlier this evening we caught  up with allison reese the executive  director  of super bowl of caring to find out how  she's inspiring viewers to help us reach  that goal this year  the inspiring piece is that in 2021  there's going to be a need for  over 14 billion meals to feed hungry  people  and because of that it's going to take  every single one of us  to help make that need  diminish think about it this way if  everybody  watching that big game uh that comes up  here in february  just gave one jar of peanut butter that  would be over a hundred million jars of  peanut butter  each one of those jars will create 15  meals  that would be 1.5 billion meals but  that's only one-tenth  of what the need is for 2021. that  really puts it in perspective  it really does alison can you explain  also to our viewers how your non-profit  acts more like a catalyst  for the food banks across the country  absolutely so super bowl of caring was  created  as a catalyst more like a movement  we have groups across the country  thousands of them each year  that participate in a food drive or  collect donations and they donated  100 locally whatever they do they decide  who's going to benefit  and then they make sure that those local  food charities  have what they need we've created a new  tackle hunger map  because right now none of us can go  volunteer or  really it's difficult to do a food drive  so the idea of the tackle hunger map  is that you can go to this place you can  see local food charities  you can help them right now through cash  donations that go  directly to those charities but in  addition to that  you know where those local charities are  and you can help them  because they all need a support network  and that's what our grassroots  effort has always been about is creating  that support network for food charities  you can find out more about this effort  of course on our website  eightnewsnow.com and we  certainly hope you can support our local  food banks with us on new year's eve
 

